WEBVTT

NOTE Timing is a draft. Re-time these cues to match the final narration audio before submission.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
The rain had softened the runway lights into long gold lines.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:16.000
In the control tower, Mara checked the weather report again.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
One aircraft remained on approach, its pilot new to night flying and quiet on the radio.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:34.000
CONTROLLER: Northstar Four-Two, wind is steady from the west. Runway lights are set to high intensity.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Continue your approach and report when you have the runway in sight.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:49.000
PILOT: Continuing. I have the lights now, but the rain is making the edges difficult to judge.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:02.000
CONTROLLER: Understood. Keep your speed stable and follow your instruments. You do not need to rush.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:10.000
If you lose the required visual reference, go around and we will set you up again.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:19.000
The pilot took a breath, checked the instruments, and made a small correction. The runway grew clearer through the rain.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:25.000
PILOT: Runway in sight. Continuing to land.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:30.000
CONTROLLER: Wind unchanged. You are cleared to land.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:43.000
The aircraft touched down smoothly. Mara watched it slow, turn off the runway, and taxi toward the terminal.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:54.000
No dramatic celebration followed. The team simply moved on to the next task, knowing that calm communication had helped bring everyone safely to the ground.
